WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.580
In this video, you tour the SUSE Virtualization dashboard and learn where to find hosts, virtual machines, images, volumes, networks, and settings.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:17.460
The dashboard opens after you log in. It shows the cluster name and version.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:24.000
Summary cards count the hosts, virtual machines, networks, images, volumes, and disks.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.780
Capacity shows how much CPU, memory, and storage is reserved and used.

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:33.970
The Events table lists recent activity in the cluster.

00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:39.240
The menu on the left leads to every resource. Select Hosts.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:45.940
Each host shows its state, IP address, and resource usage. This cluster has one host.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:52.450
Virtual Machines lists each virtual machine with its state, node, and IP address.

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:58.950
Images holds the operating system images that virtual machines boot from.

00:00:58.950 --> 00:01:02.210
Volumes lists the virtual disks.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:09.520
Networks groups virtual machine networks, cluster network configuration, and load balancers.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:17.590
Advanced holds templates, SSH keys, cloud configuration templates, storage classes, and devices.

00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:24.140
Settings holds cluster-wide options, such as the backup target.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:31.320
You now know where everything lives in the dashboard. Next, you upload a virtual machine image.
